/T (Initially, since all the slots are empty, page 3,1,2 causes a page fault and takes the empty slots  Page faults = 3  When page 1 comes, it is in the memory and no page fault occurs.  Page faults = 3  When page 6 comes, the page fault occurs, we replace the middle element i.e 1 is removed.  Page faults = 4  When page 5 comes, the page fault occurs again and middle element 6 is removed )
/E (Initially, since all the slots are empty, page 3,1,2 causes a page fault and takes the empty slots  Page faults = 3  When page 1 comes, it is in the memory and no page fault occurs.  Page faults = 3  When page 6 comes, the page fault occurs, we replace the middle element i.e 1 is removed.  Page faults = 4  When page 5 comes, the page fault occurs again and middle element 6 is removed )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
